    <task id="LOCAL-00010" summary="Developments related to completions of task of Lecture 2:&#10;&#10;1.&#9;Implemented application data saving (using serialization). All spaces, reservations and customers created during each session are saved to automatically created “Data” folder in the application main directory. The saving takes place on normal exit points of the application (upon selecting “Exit” option in Admin, Customer or Main menu). Each time the space, reservation or customer is deleted during the session, the respective files in Data folder are deleted as well.&#10;&#10;2.&#9;Implemented application data uploading (using deserialization). All spaces, reservations and customers created during the previous session are uploaded from “Data” folder upon each start of the session. That allows from continuous use of the application from session to session.&#10;&#10;3.&#9;Added custom exception “Data folder not found” extending FileNotFoundException that is thrown when the “Data” folder is deleted during the unfinished session. The exception is thrown when exiting the application upon unsuccessful attempt to save session data.&#10;&#10;4.&#9;Application classes distributed in separate packages to allow for convenient maintenance of the application.&#10;&#10;5.&#9;Customer deletion functionality added (a customer may be deleted from Administrator menu).&#10;&#10;6.&#9;Minor bugs and typos fixed.">
